<p>I think overall this idea/thread is nice but I have some slight concerns.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Open</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Close</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>What I think is great</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>The story you want to bring seems to have been thought through and definitely has some depth. You also mentioned how you plan on doing that (mostly logs and interviews) which is great. I also think the theme of guilt and your narrative compliment each other nicely.</li>
<li>I think the initial contact would make for a great discovery/addendum/&#8230;</li>
<li>You said you wanted the origin and purpose open ended which in my opinion fits the abilities and adds to the mystery of the SCP. It also makes sense since you mentioned that you plan to build more upon this in future tales and articles.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>What concerns me</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>I'm interested in how you would describe/mention how the SCP clings to the researcher. It is a bit unclear to me if you will mention this quickly or rather in detail in one of the addenda.</li>
<li>The abilities that influence time in some way or form are great but I am concerned that you will overdo it. Honestly, I'm not great with these themes/things but please know that there is a difference between complex and overcomplicated. As someone who tends to do the later I recommend you type it but always check if it affects the readability afterwards.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Final verdict</strong><br />
I compliment you for trying the combination of a guilt/isolation theme, possible time-travel,&#8230; and I think the foundations of this idea are solid but some things need a bit fleshing out.</p>
<p>I think this and the concerns in this thread can all be solved by drafting in a sandbox with a good amount of commitment, time and critique. I also advise you to check the chat and draft forums for additional help should you need it. That being said, here is a <strong><span style="color: green">second greenlight</span></strong> so you can use the draft forum. (I have an author page.)</p>
<p>Good luck with your SCP.</p>
</div>
</div>
